1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,120
Caterpillar's RSI is below thirty.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:07,000
That means oversold, not that a bottom is confirmed.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,142
The calendar lists earnings Thursday before the open.

4
00:00:10,332 --> 00:00:15,932
At the October 23 close, Caterpillar was at $687.

5
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:21,972
The weekly low at $681.23 is a support reference.

6
00:00:21,972 --> 00:00:25,772
Resistance is near $745.

7
00:00:25,772 --> 00:00:28,892
Price is below all four moving averages.

8
00:00:28,892 --> 00:00:31,934
A bounce alone would not repair that downtrend.

9
00:00:32,123 --> 00:00:35,043
RSI is 26.7.

10
00:00:35,043 --> 00:00:38,116
Friday closed below its open, with volume

11
00:00:38,116 --> 00:00:39,923
above the twenty day average.

12
00:00:39,923 --> 00:00:42,043
Selling pressure still matters.

13
00:00:42,043 --> 00:00:46,563
Average true range is about $27.38 a day.

14
00:00:46,563 --> 00:00:49,208
It describes recent movement, not a limit

15
00:00:49,208 --> 00:00:50,391
on an earnings gap.

16
00:00:50,582 --> 00:00:53,648
Recent coverage reports roughly one billion dollars

17
00:00:53,648 --> 00:00:56,962
for a North Carolina manufacturing expansion.

18
00:00:56,962 --> 00:01:00,510
The earnings test is broader: backlog, data

19
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:04,362
center power demand, margins and tariff costs.

20
00:01:04,362 --> 00:01:06,702
An investment announcement is not the same

21
00:01:06,702 --> 00:01:09,225
as orders turning into profitable revenue.

22
00:01:09,415 --> 00:01:13,415
The earnings estimate is $7.03 per share.

23
00:01:13,415 --> 00:01:17,004
The October 30 at-the-money straddle midpoint gives

24
00:01:17,004 --> 00:01:20,295
a rough 7.1 percent move in either direction.

25
00:01:20,295 --> 00:01:22,997
The bid/ask spread is wide, so this

26
00:01:22,997 --> 00:01:24,895
estimate is less precise.

27
00:01:24,895 --> 00:01:27,711
It covers risk through expiry, not just

28
00:01:27,711 --> 00:01:30,517
earnings, and the actual move can be larger.

29
00:01:30,707 --> 00:01:38,707
Holding $681.23 and reclaiming $745 would improve the chart.

30
00:01:38,707 --> 00:01:41,247
A break below support would weaken it.

31
00:01:41,247 --> 00:01:44,467
Watch the reaction and volume after the report.

32
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:46,934
These are scenarios, not predictions.

